hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2677","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, informed us Ma'mar and al-Thawri, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah (RA) that the Prophet (ﷺ) passed by him while he was lighting a fire under a cooking pot or, he said, under a pot, and lice were falling onto his face. So the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him, ""Do these lice bother you?"" He said, ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah."" Then the verse regarding fidyah (ransom) was revealed: ""Fasting for three days, or feeding six poor persons, or the slaughtering of a sheep"" (Quran 2:196).

The Prophet (ﷺ) commanded him while they were at al-Hudaybiyah, and he did not clarify to them that they would be shaving their heads there while hoping to enter Makkah. Then Allah, the Exalted, revealed the command regarding fidyah. So the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered him to shave his head and fast for three days, or feed six poor persons (a *faraq*), or sacrifice a sheep.

Abu Bakr (RA) said: The narration of Shibl from Ibn Abi Najih is also from this chapter. I have recorded it in the chapter that follows this.

**CHAPTER:**"
